{% comment %}
  Belle's Performance Tennis - When To Restring

  Long-form editorial section for templates/page.when-to-restring.json.
  Follows the same shell as belle-pricing-explainers: cream page background,
  860px container, white cards with a 12px radius, Bebas Neue headings in
  belle green, Source Sans Pro body copy.

  The argument runs in one direction and the blocks are ordered to match it:
    1. Hero, the claim (a break is a late signal)
    2. Why strings die before they snap
    3. Material comparison, poly vs natural gut
    4. Why time-based rules of thumb do not work
    5. What I do instead, the dynamic tension method
    6. Why the reading does not match the reference tension
    7. The service card
    8. What to do next

  Do not reorder 4 and 5. Block 5 only lands after the reader has accepted
  that there is no schedule that answers the question for them.

  Copy rule specific to this page: no drop-in language. Every ask is
  "make an appointment" (block 8 and the cta-inline below it). Do not
  reintroduce "bring it by" or "come by". There is a fixed location for
  the reading appointment, but it is deliberately NOT named here, see
  BRAND.md on not publishing a base address. If a location is ever added
  it belongs in the booking flow, not in this copy.

  Copy is hardcoded rather than schema-driven, same as the pricing
  explainers section. There is deliberately no CTA button inside this
  section: the page closes with cta-inline, and an in-section button sat
  directly above it as a duplicate. Same call that was made on the pricing
  page. Add one back only if it moves somewhere higher up the page.
{% endcomment %}

